## 6) Important note: make toggle actually affect blocking

The above popup toggles state, but the ruleset remains active. To make the toggle work, you can use **enabled rulesets** or **dynamic rules**.

Here’s a simple improvement using `updateEnabledRulesets()`.

### Replace `background.js` with:

```js
chrome.runtime.onInstalled.addListener(async () => {
  await chrome.storage.sync.set({ blockingEnabled: true });
  await chrome.declarativeNetRequest.updateEnabledRulesets({
    enableRulesetIds: ["tracking_rules"]
  });
});

chrome.storage.onChanged.addListener(async (changes, areaName) => {
  if (areaName !== "sync" || !changes.blockingEnabled) return;

  const enabled = changes.blockingEnabled.newValue;

  await chrome.declarativeNetRequest.updateEnabledRulesets({
    enableRulesetIds: enabled ? ["tracking_rules"] : [],
    disableRulesetIds: enabled ? [] : ["tracking_rules"]
  });
});
```

