This initializes extension state and can be used later for dynamic rule management.

```js
chrome.runtime.onInstalled.addListener(() => {
  chrome.storage.local.set({
    enabled: true,
    blockedRequests: 0
  });
});

chrome.declarativeNetRequest.onRuleMatchedDebug?.addListener((info) => {
  chrome.storage.local.get(["blockedRequests"], (data) => {
    const current = data.blockedRequests || 0;
    chrome.storage.local.set({ blockedRequests: current + 1 });
  });
});
```

> Note: `onRuleMatchedDebug` may require additional debugging permissions in some environments and is not always available in production. If it causes issues, remove it for now.

