## Important note about enabling/disabling blocking

The static rules above are always active. If you want the toggle to actually enable/disable blocking, you should use **dynamic rules** or update the ruleset state via `declarativeNetRequest.updateEnabledRulesets()`.

Here’s a simple approach in `background.js`:

```js
chrome.runtime.onInstalled.addListener(() => {
  chrome.storage.sync.get(["enabled"], (result) => {
    const enabled = result.enabled !== false;
    chrome.declarativeNetRequest.updateEnabledRulesets({
      enableRulesetIds: enabled ? ["static_rules"] : [],
      disableRulesetIds: enabled ? [] : ["static_rules"]
    });
  });
});

chrome.storage.onChanged.addListener((changes, areaName) => {
  if (areaName === "sync" && changes.enabled) {
    const enabled = changes.enabled.newValue !== false;
    chrome.declarativeNetRequest.updateEnabledRulesets({
      enableRulesetIds: enabled ? ["static_rules"] : [],
      disableRulesetIds: enabled ? [] : ["static_rules"]
    });
  }
});
```

