## Replacing simulated data with real data

If you want real-time stock prices:
- Connect to a **WebSocket** feed
- Or poll a REST API every few seconds
- Update `stocks[i].price`, `changePct`, and `volume`
- Call `draw()` after updates

Example pattern:

```js
const ws = new WebSocket("wss://your-feed.example.com");

ws.onmessage = (event) => {
  const updates = JSON.parse(event.data);
  for (const u of updates) {
    const stock = stocks.find(s => s.symbol === u.symbol);
    if (stock) {
      stock.prevPrice = stock.price;
      stock.price = u.price;
      stock.changePct = ((stock.price - stock.prevPrice) / stock.prevPrice) * 100;
      stock.volume = u.volume ?? stock.volume;
    }
  }
  draw();
};
```

