## How to connect a real-time data source

Replace the `setInterval(updatePrices, 1000)` simulation with a WebSocket:

```js
const ws = new WebSocket('wss://your-feed.example.com');

ws.onmessage = (event) => {
  const updates = JSON.parse(event.data);
  // Example update format:
  // [{ symbol: "AAPL", price: 234.12, volume: 1234567 }, ...]
  for (const u of updates) {
    const cell = cells.find(c => c.symbol === u.symbol);
    if (cell) {
      cell.prevClose = cell.prevClose ?? cell.price;
      cell.price = u.price;
      if (u.volume != null) cell.volume = u.volume;
    }
  }
  recalcChanges();
  draw();
};
```

