You can replace the simulated `setInterval(...)` block with a WebSocket or polling API call. For example:

```js
const ws = new WebSocket("wss://your-feed.example.com");
ws.onmessage = (event) => {
  const updates = JSON.parse(event.data);
  // merge updates into state.stocks
  draw();
};
```

