## Latency
- Avoid blocking I/O on the hot path
- Use async carefully; not everything should be async if it adds overhead
- Pre-allocate objects where possible
- Keep strategy state local and in-memory

## Reliability
- Idempotent order handling
- Sequence numbers for market data and order events
- Replay support from event logs
- Circuit breakers for venue connectivity

## Risk
- Hard pre-trade limits
- Kill switch
- Max order rate
- Max position per symbol
- Max daily loss

## Observability
- End-to-end latency per order
- Market data lag
- Queue depth
- Rejection reasons
- Fill ratios
