## Why this is fast

### 1. Open addressing
Avoids pointer chasing and heap allocations typical of chained hash maps.

### 2. Fixed-size records
Keeps memory layout predictable and cache-friendly.

### 3. No dynamic allocation per packet
Only the table is allocated up front.

### 4. Simple key hashing
Fast enough for high-throughput flow tracking.

### 5. Batch-friendly aging
Aging can be run periodically rather than on every packet.

