## Example: simple integer-to-string helper

If your environment doesn’t support `snprintf`, use this:

```c
static void u16_to_str(uint16_t value, char *buf)
{
    char temp[6];
    int i = 0, j = 0;

    if (value == 0) {
        buf[0] = '0';
        buf[1] = '\0';
        return;
    }

    while (value > 0 && i < 5) {
        temp[i++] = (char)('0' + (value % 10));
        value /= 10;
    }

    while (i > 0) {
        buf[j++] = temp[--i];
    }
    buf[j] = '\0';
}
