## 1) Pipeline design

### Data flow
```text
Accelerometer ISR / driver
        ↓
Sample queue / ring buffer
        ↓
Preprocessing (magnitude, smoothing)
        ↓
Feature extraction (mean, variance, delta)
        ↓
Anomaly scoring
        ↓
Event generation / logging / alert
```

### Initial anomaly logic
A sample is considered anomalous if the filtered magnitude deviates from the rolling baseline by more than a threshold for a minimum number of consecutive samples.

This is a good starting point for:
- shocks
- drops
- unusual vibration
- sudden motion spikes

